## Problem

probe-rs has many loops of the same shape: poll the target, give up once a timeout has passed, otherwise sleep a millisecond and poll again. [`wait_for_core_halted`](https://github.com/probe-rs/probe-rs/blob/07e777d423ec86ad0b050a89c0fcb7501ee85b5a/probe-rs/src/architecture/arm/core/armv7ar.rs#L488) is one:

```rust
let start = Instant::now();

while !core_halted(memory, base_address)? {
    if start.elapsed() >= timeout {
        return Err(ArmError::Timeout);
    }
    // Wait a bit before polling again.
    std::thread::sleep(Duration::from_millis(1));
}
```

The success path is tested. [`armv7a_wait_for_core_halted`](https://github.com/probe-rs/probe-rs/blob/07e777d423ec86ad0b050a89c0fcb7501ee85b5a/probe-rs/src/architecture/arm/core/armv7ar.rs#L2223) queues one "running" read and one "halted" read, and the loop halts on the second poll.

